      "spec_gap": true,
      "suggested_fix": "WHEN the checkout calls `pricing.tips.tip_cents(-1005, 10)` THEN it returns `-101`.",
      "id": "F-2c3804c2"
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "title": "Very large totals raise decimal.InvalidOperation",
      "detail": "The code uses the default decimal context, which has 28 digits of precision. When the tip has more than 28 integer digits, quantize(Decimal('1')) raises decimal.InvalidOperation instead of returning an int. For example, tip_cents(10**30, 10) should be 10**29 (30 digits) but raises. A plain integer implementation would return the exact value. The spec does not limit the input range.",
